  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/we100-1000.html",
  "prefLabel": "We 101.19 Hydrofracturing",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "We 101.19 “Hydrofracturing” means a well development technique capable of utilizing a minimum water pressure of 2000 pounds per square inch and minimum pumping flow rate of 35 gallons per minute and one or more inflatable or mechanical packers to flush out or expand fractures within a well.\n\nSource. #6448, eff 1-29-97; ss by #7306, eff 6-13-00; ss by #9177, eff 6-13-08 (from We 101.16); renumbered by #12075 (formerly We 101.17)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/we100-1000.html"
